(On Public Reading Rooms) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A reading room is a promise made by a town to every person who walks through its door.) Tj T*
(The promise is simple: knowledge kept on a shelf belongs to anyone who can reach for it.) Tj T*
(In the town of Samarpur the first reading room opened in 1921 in two rented rooms above) Tj T*
(a grain shop. It held four hundred books, three newspapers and a single lamp. The) Tj T*
(committee that ran it wrote in its first report that the doors must open before the) Tj T*
(mills began their shifts and close after they ended, so that workers could read on the) Tj T*
(way to work and on the way home.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
