(The committee kept a register of every borrower. By 1925 the register listed more than) Tj T*
(eleven hundred names, and nearly half of the borrowers had signed with a thumb) Tj T*
(impression when they first joined. The committee organised evening classes so that) Tj T*
(members could learn to read the books they borrowed. The report of 1926 says that a) Tj T*
(reading room should be judged not by the number of books on its shelves but by the) Tj T*
(number of people who leave able to read a book they could not read before.) Tj T*
